# Furtive Courier: "can't be blocked as long as you've sacrificed an artifact this turn" (CR 611.3a): it is only this turn that counts. Turn 1 Bot1 casts a
# Black Lotus and sacrifices it for the Courier, so on turn 3 it has sacrificed nothing this turn: Bot2's Grizzly Bears blocks, and both die. The loot
# on the attack draws the Plains and Bot1 discards the Swamp.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Furtive Courier
Island
Forest
Mountain
Island
Island
Swamp
Plains
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Furtive Courier.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Furtive Courier > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Swamp)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Grizzly Bears > Furtive Courier)
[T3 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Mountain; Island; Island; Plains
Bot1.Graveyard = Furtive Courier; Swamp; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Grizzly Bears
